.TH CAUDIO 1 "2026-09-14" "caudio 0.25.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
caudio \- C++23 headless music player daemon and CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B caudio
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
\fISUBCOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]...
.br
.B caudio
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
\fBstart\fR [\fB\-\-foreground\fR]
.br
.B caudio
\fBseek\fR \fITIME\fR
.br
.B caudio
\fBvolume\fR [\fILEVEL\fR]
.br
.B caudio
\fBqueue\fR \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
.br
.B caudio
\fBplaylist\fR \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
.br
.B caudio
\fBlibrary\fR \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
.br
.B caudio
\fBconfig\fR \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
.br
.B caudio
\fBtag\fR \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
.br
.B caudio
\fBhistory\fR \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
.br
.B caudio
\fBdevice\fR \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B caudio
is a C++23 headless music player. It consists of a background daemon
(\fBcaudio start\fR) and a CLI that communicates with the daemon over a
local IPC channel (Unix Domain Socket on POSIX, Named Pipe on Windows)
using a JSON protocol with a 4\-byte big\-endian length prefix.
Audio decoding uses FFmpeg (libavformat/avcodec/avutil/swresample).
The library is split into modules: \fBcaudio::utils\fR, \fBcaudio::player\fR,
\fBcaudio::db\fR, \fBcaudio::engine\fR, plus \fBcaudio::cli\fR/\fBservice\fR/\fBclient\fR.
.PP
Shared\-memory status (\fBAtomicShmStatus\fR) is published at 10 fps for
low\-latency TUI polling without IPC round\-trips.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-config " \fIFILE\fR"
Config file path. Default is XDG config home on POSIX
(\fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/caudio/config.json\fR or \fB~/.config/caudio/config.json\fR)
and \fB%LOCALAPPDATA%/caudio/config.json\fR on Windows.
.TP
.BR \-\-log\-level " \fILEVEL\fR"
Daemon log level: \fBtrace\fR|\fBdebug\fR|\fBinfo\fR|\fBwarn\fR|\fBerror\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-device " \fIDEVICE\fR"
Audio output device ID. Overrides config.
.TP
.BR \-\-version
Show version (\fBcaudio::kVersionFull\fR, e.g. \fBv0.25.4\fR) and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-daemon ", " \-\-foreground
Internal daemon flags. Do not pass manually; used by \fBcaudio start\fR
when spawning the background process.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Daemon lifecycle
.TP
.B start [\-\-foreground]
Start daemon. By default spawns a background process (fork/CreateProcess
with \fBDETACHED_PROCESS\fR) and polls for socket readiness. With
\fB\-\-foreground\fR runs in the foreground (for systemd or debugging).
Creates DB parent directories if needed and derives the socket path
from the DB path via \fBcaudio::cli::socketPathFor\fR.
.TP
.B shutdown
Stop daemon. Sends \fBShutdown\fR IPC command and polls for socket and
pid file removal. Reports an error if the daemon is still running.
.SS Playback control
.TP
.B play
Start playback. If paused, resumes;
if playing
    , restarts;
if stopped,
starts from queue head.
.TP
.B pause
Pause playback, preserving position.
.TP
.B resume
Resume from paused position.
.TP
.B restart
Seek to 0 and ensure playing state.
.TP
.B stop
Stop playback and clear current track.
.TP
.B next
Advance to next track. Handles \fBRepeatMode::One\fR and shuffle.
.TP
.B prev
Go to previous track.
.TP
.B seek \fITIME\fR
Seek to position. \fITIME\fR can be absolute (\fBmm:ss\fR or seconds,
e.g. \fB1:30\fR or \fB90\fR) or relative (\fB+N\fR/\fB\-N\fR). Relative
seeks fetch current position via \fBStatusReq\fR and clamp to 0.
.TP
.B status [\-\-json] [\-\-watch] [\-\-follow] [\-\-interval \fIMS\fR]
Show playback status (state, position, duration, volume, shuffle,
repeat, track id/title/artist/path, queue size/index). \fB\-\-json\fR
emits JSON. \fB\-\-watch\fR/\fB\-\-follow\fR polls continuously every
\fB\-\-interval\fR ms (default 1000) with timestamps in text mode or
compact JSON per line in JSON mode.
.TP
.B volume [\fILEVEL\fR]
Get or set volume. \fILEVEL\fR: \fB0\fR\-100 (absolute), \fB+N\fR/\fB\-N\fR
(delta), \fBmute\fR/\fBunmute\fR. No argument prints current volume.
.TP
.B info [\-\-json]
Show detailed info for the currently playing track (metadata + play
statistics).
.SS Queue
.TP
.B queue list [\-\-json]
List tracks in the active queue.
.TP
.B queue queues
List all queues with track counts.
.TP
.B queue switch \fIQID\fR
Switch active queue by ID. Engine validates that the queue exists.
.TP
.B queue add \fIQUERY\fR [\-\-search]
Add to queue. \fIQUERY\fR is interpreted as file path, track ID, or
FTS query. \fB\-\-search\fR forces FTS search. New files are fingerprinted
(BLAKE3).
.TP
.B queue remove \fIID\fR
Remove from queue by queue position or track ID.
.TP
.B queue move \fIFROM\fR \fITO\fR
Move track within queue from index \fIFROM\fR to \fITO\fR (atomic
clear+re\-enqueue transaction).
.TP
.B queue clear
Clear entire queue atomically.
.TP
.B queue shuffle [\fIon\fR|\fIoff\fR]
Set shuffle mode. No argument toggles.
.TP
.B queue repeat [\fIoff\fR|\fIone\fR|\fIall\fR]
Set repeat mode. No argument shows current mode. \fBall\fR maps to
\fBRepeatMode::Queue\fR.
.SS Playlist
.TP
.B playlist list [\-\-json]
List all playlists.
.TP
.B playlist tracks \fIPID\fR
List tracks in playlist \fIPID\fR.
.TP
.B playlist load \fIPID\fR [\-\-play]
Load playlist \fIPID\fR into the queue (clears first). With \fB\-\-play\fR
starts playback.
.TP
.B playlist save \fINAME\fR [\-\-queue \fIQID\fR]
Save queue as a new playlist named \fINAME\fR. Optionally specify queue
ID (default active queue).
.TP
.B playlist delete \fIPID\fR
Delete playlist \fIPID\fR.
.TP
.B playlist rename \fIPID\fR \fINAME\fR
Rename playlist \fIPID\fR to \fINAME\fR.
.TP
.B playlist export \fIPID\fR \fIPATH\fR [\-\-format m3u|pls|json]
Export playlist \fIPID\fR to file \fIPATH\fR. Formats: \fBm3u\fR (default),
\fBpls\fR, \fBjson\fR.
.TP
.B playlist import \fIPATH\fR [\-\-name \fINAME\fR]
Import playlist from file \fIPATH\fR. If \fB\-\-name\fR omitted, derived
from filename.
.SS Library
.TP
.B library scan [\-\-path \fIPATH\fR] [\-\-mode sampled|full]
Scan library for audio files. Default path is the music directory
adjacent to the DB. \fBsampled\fR (fast, first/last 64 KiB) or
\fBfull\fR (entire file) for BLAKE3 fingerprint.
.TP
.B library search \fIQUERY\fR [\-\-limit \fIN\fR] [\-\-json]
FTS5 search with \fBLIKE\fR fallback. Default limit 50.
.TP
.B library stats [\-\-json] [\-\-detailed]
Show library counts (tracks/queues/playlists). With \fB\-\-detailed\fR
includes most\-played and total play time.
.TP
.B library list [\-\-query \fIQ\fR] [\-\-artist \fIA\fR] [\-\-album \fIA\fR] [\-\-genre \fIG\fR] [\-\-limit \fIN\fR] [\-\-offset \fIN\fR] [\-\-json]
List library tracks with optional filtering and pagination.
.TP
.B library add \fIPATH\fR [\-\-recursive]
Add file or directory to library with metadata extraction.
.TP
.B library remove \fIID\fR
Remove track from library by ID or path.
.SS Tags
.TP
.B tag edit \fIID\fR \fIFIELD\fR \fIVALUE\fR
Edit track tag. \fIFIELD\fR: \fBtitle\fR|\fBartist\fR|\fBalbum\fR|\fBalbum_artist\fR|\fBgenre\fR|\fByear\fR|\fBtrack_number\fR|\fBdisc_number\fR.
.TP
.B tag get \fIID\fR [\-\-json]
Get track tags for track \fIID\fR.
.SS History
.TP
.B history list [\-\-limit \fIN\fR] [\-\-json]
List playback history. Default limit 50.
.TP
.B history clear
Clear playback history.
.SS Device
.TP
.B device list [\-\-json]
List audio output devices (via miniaudio enumeration).
.TP
.B device set \fIID\fR
Set default audio output device.
.TP
.B device test [\-\-id \fIID\fR]
Test audio device by playing a tone. Defaults to current config device.
.SS Config
.TP
.B config get \fIKEY\fR
Get config value for \fIKEY\fR.
.TP
.B config set \fIKEY\fR \fIVALUE\fR
Set config value. \fIVALUE\fR is stored as JSON or plain string.
.TP
.B config list [\-\-json]
List all config key/value pairs.
.TP
.B config export \fIPATH\fR
Copy config file to \fIPATH\fR.
.TP
.B config import \fIPATH\fR
Copy file at \fIPATH\fR to config location.
.TP
.B config reset [\fIKEY\fR]
Reset config \fIKEY\fR or all keys to defaults.
.SS Preview and TUI
.TP
.B preview \fIFILE\fR
Ephemeral playback of \fIFILE\fR without daemon (direct \fBcaudio::player::Player\fR).
Blocks until playback finishes.
.TP
.B tui
Launch TUI preview. Ensures daemon is running, prints current status,
and shows guidance. Full ratatui TUI is planned for v0.28.0. For live
polling use \fBcaudio status \-\-watch\fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Start daemon and play a file:
.B caudio start;
caudio queue add ~/ Music / album / track.flac;
caudio play;
caudio status.TP Search and queue :.B caudio library search
                                   "beatles" --limit 10 .br.B caudio queue add
                                   "beatles" --search.br.B caudio next; caudio status --json
.TP
Library scan and stats:
.B caudio library scan --path ~/Music --mode sampled
.br
.B caudio library stats --detailed --json
.TP
Live status polling (for scripts/TUI):
.B caudio status --watch --interval 200
.TP
Volume control:
.B caudio volume 75;
caudio volume + 5;
caudio volume mute;
caudio volume.TP Playlist workflows :.B caudio playlist save "My Mix";
caudio playlist export 1 / tmp / mix.m3u-- format m3u.br.B caudio playlist import / tmp /
        mix.m3u-- name "Imported".SH FILES.TP.I ~/.config / caudio / config.json(POSIX).TP.I
        % LOCALAPPDATA %\\caudio\\config.json(Windows) Default config file.Overridden by \fB\-\-
    config\fR.Stores DB path,
    socket path, device, log level,
    etc..TP.I ~/.local / share / caudio / caudio.db(POSIX).TP.I % LOCALAPPDATA
        %\\caudio\\caudio.db(Windows) Default SQLite database path.Contains tracks,
    queues, playlists, history,
    FTS5 index.Parent directories are created automatically..TP.I / tmp / caudio -
            <hash>.sock(POSIX).TP.I \\\\.\\pipe\\caudio -
            <hash>(Windows) IPC socket /
                named pipe
                    .Canonical path derived from DB path hash via
\fBcaudio::cli::socketPathFor\fR.Hash is BLAKE3 of the DB path..TP.I
                / tmp / caudio
            - <hash>.pid
        or % LOCALAPPDATA % / caudio /
                   caudio.pid Daemon pid file
                       .Path derived from DB path via \fBcaudio::cli::pidPathFor\fR..TP.I
                   / dev / shm / caudio
               - <hash>(POSIX) or
        named shared memory(Windows)
SHM status block (\fBAtomicShmStatus\fR) for 10 fps TUI polling.
